# .env - bootstrap only. Copy to .env. Never committed.
#
# This file is NOT configuration. It holds the two things ssmd must know before it
# can read its configuration, plus secret material that must never be committed.
# Everything else - ports, image tags, timeouts, service selection, hooks, agent
# limits - lives in the config database and is edited with `ssmd config set` or by
# editing config/*.yml.
#
# If you are about to add a setting here, it almost certainly belongs in
# config/stack.yml (project-wide) or config/hosts.yml (machine-specific).
# Check first:   ssmd config list

# ── where the configuration is ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The SQLite store, relative to the dev-stack directory or absolute. Seeded from
# config/*.yml on first run and re-seeded whenever one of them changes.
# SSMD_DB=config/ssmd.db

# Which host profile in config/hosts.yml applies to this machine. This is the
# one value that legitimately differs per developer, and it is a selector rather
# than a setting: the values it selects are all in config/hosts.yml, committed.
#
#   ssmd config hosts      lists what is available
#   local      loopback-only; a laptop or workstation
#   vm         a shared dev VM reached over the LAN or an SSH tunnel
#   alt-ports  a machine already running something else on 80/443
#   ci         no published ports, nothing interactive
SSMD_HOST=local

# ── secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Injected into containers, never stored in the config database and never
# printed by `ssmd config list`. Leave unset if you do not need them.

# For private package repositories, and to lift GitHub's anonymous rate limit.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Passed into agent sandboxes. Leave unset to drive an agent from the host
# instead - a key that never enters the container cannot be exfiltrated from it.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Override the local object-storage credentials if you have a reason to.
# S3_KEY=
# S3_SECRET=

# ── escape hatches ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Who the audit trail attributes actions to. Set automatically by the MCP server
# and the agent sandbox; set it by hand only when impersonating one for a test.
# SSMD_ACTOR=

# Answer yes to every confirmation. For CI. An agent cannot set this for itself -
# it must already be in the environment ssmd was invoked with.
# SSMD_YES=1
